# What NOT to upload to Vercel. This replaces .gitignore for the CLI's upload,
# so the ordinary build junk has to be repeated here.
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.log
*.local
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The 19MB of dead sprite sheets that used to be excluded here now live in
# docs/unused-art/ instead, and this file no longer has anything to say about
# them. That move is deliberate and this comment is the reason:
#
# .vercelignore ONLY APPLIES TO CLI UPLOADS. The project is connected to the
# GitHub repo for auto-deploys, and a Git deployment clones the repo rather
# than uploading from disk — so an exclusion listed here would have been
# silently ignored and the dead art would have gone straight back into every
# player's first load. Keeping them out of `public/` works for both paths,
# because Vite only ever copies `public/` into `dist`.
#
# Don't re-add art exclusions here. Move the file instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 19MB of reference sheets the game never loads. Fine in the repo, no reason to
# upload them on a CLI deploy either.
docs/unused-art
